# Keep host build artifacts and local cruft out of the image build context.
#
# The important one is obj/ and bin/: the Dockerfile does `dotnet restore` then `COPY src/ src/`, and a host
# obj/project.assets.json carries a Windows fallback package folder
# ('C:\Program Files (x86)\Microsoft Visual Studio\Shared\NuGetPackages') that does not exist in the Linux build
# image — copying it over clobbers the container's clean restore and `dotnet publish --no-restore` then fails with
# "Unable to find fallback package folder". Excluding these makes the build reproducible from any working tree.

# .NET build output
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Python venvs, caches, and the tag-model artifacts (fetched at runtime, never built into the image)
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
tagmodel/artifacts/

# VCS, local config, editor/IDE state
.git/
.env
*.user
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
